    "note": "Filed: 65,000 ft, 460 mph (FlightAware). Actual: climbed to FL600, held there almost the whole flight; mission ran ~3h10m, about half the 6h12m filed plan. Staged out of Great Falls, MT -- not its normal Edwards AFB/NASA Armstrong base.",
    "pattern": "Confirmed by Alex (2026-08-01) as tied to the Silvertip Fire (Bob Marshall Wilderness / Flathead NF, MT — ~4,142 ac, Type 4 IC confine/monitor). Mission complete, landed back at Great Falls. Recorded track (real, from globe.airplanes.live) shows it climbed out over Silvertip itself -- 3.3 mi closest approach at 58,400 ft -- then transited to fly a racetrack survey pattern at FL600 directly over the Okanogan/Colville fire complex in WA (Kaiser Canyon, Sinlahekin, etc.) before returning. Filed route's VOR-radial and named-fix legs were never plotted (no confirmed coordinates for them); the recorded track now shown is the real flown path, not the filed one."
